<!-- ── 01 SOROLLA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="artist" id="sorolla">
  <div class="artist-header">
    <span class="artist-num">01</span>
    <div class="artist-nameblock">
      <h2 class="artist-name">Joaquín Sorolla</h2>
      <p class="artist-meta">b. 1863, Valencia, Spain &nbsp;·&nbsp; d. 1923, Cercedilla &nbsp;·&nbsp; Spanish</p>
      <span class="artist-tag">Spanish Impressionism</span>
      <span class="artist-tag">Luminism</span>
      <span class="artist-tag">Plein Air</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="fields">
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">Artist Statement</span>
      <p class="field-value serif">"I do not paint sadness. I believe only in light."</p>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">Practice</span>
      <p class="field-value">지중해 해변의 빛·물·인물을 그린 루미니즘 회화의 거장. 야외 직접 제작(plein air)으로 햇빛 아래 색채와 형태의 변화를 포착했다. 대표작 〈슬픈 유산〉(1900 파리 만국박람회 대상), 〈해변의 산책〉, 히스패닉 소사이어티 벽화 연작 〈스페인의 환영〉(14점, 227m²). 2,000점 이상의 작품을 남겼으며 마드리드 소로야 미술관(옛 작업실 자택)이 최대 컬렉션을 보유한다.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">주요 전시</span>
      <ul class="exh-list">
        <li class="exh-item"><span class="exh-year">2026</span>《A Living Vision: the Sorolla Gallery at 100》 Hispanic Society of America, New York <span class="exh-venue">2026.5.21–2027.5.27</span></li>
        <li class="exh-item"><span class="exh-year">2026</span>《소로야의 바다》 Palau Martorell, Barcelona <span class="exh-venue">2025.12–2026.4</span></li>
        <li class="exh-item"><span class="exh-year">2026</span>반카하 재단, 발렌시아 — 소로야 미술관 걸작 60점 순회 <span class="exh-venue">2025.10–2026.4</span></li>
        <li class="exh-item"><span class="exh-year">2009</span>New York Hispanic Society solo — 160,000명 방문, 이후 루스벨트·태프트 대통령 초상 위촉</li>
        <li class="exh-item"><span class="exh-year">1900</span>Grand Prix, Exposition Universelle, Paris</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">경매가</span>
      <table class="price-table">
        <thead><tr><th>연도</th><th>작품</th><th>경매사</th><th>낙찰가</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>2012</td><td>Pescadores Valencianos</td><td>Sotheby's London</td><td>£4.0M (~$5.95M) — 경매 최고가</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2019</td><td>El bote blanco, Jávea</td><td>Sotheby's NY</td><td>$2.89M</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2018</td><td>Barcas de pesca en la playa</td><td>Christie's London</td><td>£1.56M</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2021</td><td>Valencia, la pesca de la tarde</td><td>Sotheby's NY</td><td>$1.02M</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">웹사이트 / 갤러리</span>
      <div class="link-row">
        <a class="link-btn primary" href="https://www.museosorolla.es" target="_blank">museosorolla.es</a>
        <a class="link-btn" href="https://www.hispanicsociety.org" target="_blank">Hispanic Society of America</a>
        <a class="link-btn" href="https://www.artnet.com/artists/joaquin-sorolla-y-bastida/" target="_blank">Artnet</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">대표 작품</span>
      <div class="artwork-grid">
      <figure class="artwork-fig">
        <div class="artwork-img-wrap">
          <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Joaqu%C3%ADn_Sorolla_y_Bastida_-_Strolling_along_the_Seashore_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/960px-Joaqu%C3%ADn_Sorolla_y_Bastida_-_Strolling_along_the_Seashore_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" alt="Strolling Along the Seashore, 1909" loading="lazy"
            onerror="this.parentElement.innerHTML='<div class=img-fail>이미지 로드 실패</div>'">
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <p class="artwork-caption">〈해변의 산책 / Strolling Along the Seashore〉, 1909. Oil on canvas, 200 × 205 cm. Museo Sorolla, Madrid.</p>
          <div class="artwork-meta">
            <span class="artwork-copyright">Public Domain — Wikimedia Commons / Google Art Project</span>
            <a class="artwork-source" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joaqu%C3%ADn_Sorolla_y_Bastida_-_Strolling_along_the_Seashore_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">원문 ↗</a>
          </div>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="artwork-fig">
        <div class="artwork-img-wrap">
          <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Joaquin_Sorolla_-_Ni%C3%B1os_en_la_playa.jpg/900px-Joaquin_Sorolla_-_Ni%C3%B1os_en_la_playa.jpg" alt="Niños en la playa, 1910" loading="lazy"
            onerror="this.parentElement.innerHTML='<div class=img-fail>이미지 로드 실패</div>'">
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <p class="artwork-caption">〈해변의 아이들 / Niños en la playa〉, 1910. Oil on canvas, 118 × 185 cm. Museo del Prado, Madrid.</p>
          <div class="artwork-meta">
            <span class="artwork-copyright">Public Domain — Wikimedia Commons</span>
            <a class="artwork-source" href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joaquin_Sorolla_-_Ni%C3%B1os_en_la_playa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">원문 ↗</a>
          </div>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<!-- ── 02 LONGEVIAL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="artist" id="longevial">
  <div class="artist-header">
    <span class="artist-num">02</span>
    <div class="artist-nameblock">
      <h2 class="artist-name">Inès Longevial</h2>
      <p class="artist-meta">b. 1990, Agen, France &nbsp;·&nbsp; Lives: Paris &nbsp;·&nbsp; French</p>
      <span class="artist-tag">Figurative Painting</span>
      <span class="artist-tag">Fauvism</span>
      <span class="artist-tag">Self-Portrait</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="fields">
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">Artist Statement</span>
      <p class="field-value serif">"Naturally, I was very attracted by the cliché and idealistic representation of the female body — like so many that are posted on Instagram. I wanted to counter that with something more truthful: the forgotten forms of flesh."</p>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">Practice</span>
      <p class="field-value">포비즘(Fauvism) 색채를 바탕으로 한 생동감 넘치는 구상 회화. 자화상과 여성 신체의 파편(손끝, 광대뼈, 눈두덩) — 사회가 요구하는 이상화된 신체 대신, 일상에서 잊혀온 살의 형태를 그린다. 빛의 변주와 피부톤·그림자 탐구를 통해 자기 신체와 여성성을 되찾는 작업이다. 소셜미디어를 통해 초기 인지도를 쌓았으며, 알민 레쉬 전속과 리졸리 모노그래프 출판으로 기관적 위상을 확립했다. 피카소·로댕·카미유 클로델을 주요 영향으로 꼽는다.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">주요 전시</span>
      <ul class="exh-list">
        <li class="exh-item"><span class="exh-year">2025</span>《Skin of a Storm》 Almine Rech, Tribeca, New York</li>
        <li class="exh-item"><span class="exh-year">2024</span>《Visages》 Almine Rech, New York &nbsp;·&nbsp; 《Les Silences du Désir》 Almine Rech, Shanghai &nbsp;·&nbsp; 《Le Jour des peintres》 Musée d'Orsay, Paris</li>
        <li class="exh-item"><span class="exh-year">2023</span>《Pourfendue》 Almine Rech, London &nbsp;·&nbsp; 《Perchée》 Ketabi Bourdet, Paris</li>
        <li class="exh-item"><span class="exh-year">2022</span>《En chair et en os》 Van de Weghe, New York &nbsp;·&nbsp; 《L'Heure Magique》 Musée des Beaux-Arts d'Agen</li>
        <li class="exh-item"><span class="exh-year">2018</span>《Sous Le Soleil》 HVW8, Los Angeles — 미국 첫 개인전; Juxtapoz 2018 봄호 표지</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">경매가</span>
      <p class="field-value">2차 경매 기록 제한적. Artnet 기재 작품: <em>Olive Oil on Dragon Fruit</em> (2022) 경매 — 갤러리 1차 시장 중심. 소형 작품 약 €5,000–€15,000, 대형 회화 갤러리가 €30,000+ 추정. 알민 레쉬 전속 이후 시장 형성 가속 중.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">웹사이트 / 갤러리</span>
      <div class="link-row">
        <a class="link-btn primary" href="https://www.ineslongevial.com" target="_blank">ineslongevial.com</a>
        <a class="link-btn" href="https://www.alminerech.com/artists/292-ines-longevial" target="_blank">Almine Rech</a>
        <a class="link-btn" href="https://www.ketabibourdet.com/artists/25-ines-longevial-b.-1990/" target="_blank">Ketabi Bourdet</a>
        <a class="link-btn" href="https://www.artnet.com/artists/in%C3%A8s-longevial/" target="_blank">Artnet</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">대표 작품</span>
      <div class="artwork-grid">
      <figure class="artwork-fig">
        <div class="artwork-img-wrap">
          <img src="https://ocula.com/media/uploads/artworks/ines-longevial-untitled-2022.jpg" alt="Inès Longevial painting" loading="lazy"
            onerror="this.parentElement.innerHTML='<div class=img-fail>이미지 로드 실패</div>'">
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <p class="artwork-caption">Inès Longevial, 〈Untitled〉, 2022. Oil on canvas. Almine Rech.</p>
          <div class="artwork-meta">
            <span class="artwork-copyright">© Inès Longevial. Courtesy Almine Rech.</span>
            <a class="artwork-source" href="https://ocula.com/artists/ines-longevial/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">원문 ↗</a>
          </div>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<!-- ── 03 MUNTEAN / ROSENBLUM ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="artist" id="muntean">
  <div class="artist-header">
    <span class="artist-num">03</span>
    <div class="artist-nameblock">
      <h2 class="artist-name">Muntean / Rosenblum</h2>
      <p class="artist-meta">Markus Muntean b. 1962 Graz, Austria &nbsp;·&nbsp; Adi Rosenblum b. 1962 Haifa, Israel &nbsp;·&nbsp; Collaboration since 1992 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Vienna / London / Tel Aviv</p>
      <span class="artist-tag">Figurative Painting</span>
      <span class="artist-tag">Video / Installation</span>
      <span class="artist-tag">Neo-Conceptualism</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="fields">
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">Artist Statement</span>
      <p class="field-value serif">"We are interested in the gap between what we are told life should be and what it actually is — the young people we paint occupy that gap."</p>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <span class="field-label">Practice</span>
